{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Every male from a month old</b> and so on. The reason for 'from a month old' is according to the time when they [the Levites] came in their stead — they being the firstborns — for why should the firstborn give his redemption once there is a Levite son in his place? And if you say: why do the Levites not likewise redeem the firstborns from then onward, so that Israel would not need redemption for their firstborns? — one may answer that those Levites had already entered in place of the firstborns who existed then, and HaShem established their sons in place of their fathers, for they and their sons were sanctified forever. And perhaps it is for this that HaShem doubled His statement in what He wrote in the verse: <b>ואני הנה לקחתי את הלוים</b> — 'and I, behold, I have taken the Levites' — and so on, <b>והיו לי הלוים</b> — 'and the Levites shall be Mine' — meaning, they and their sons' sons were definitively fixed; from now on there is no Levite to redeem a firstborn of Israel born afterward as the one who opens the womb."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:05:55.499927360Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}